Run a hook as a worker's wasm thread ends

A worker's wasm thread ends when wasm_thread_entry_point returns, after
which the worker closes. Code that keeps state per wasm thread, such as a
per-thread allocator heap, needs to release it then, while the thread's
thread-local storage is still valid; nothing else marks that moment, as
a parked worker keeps its wasm thread across the threads it runs.

